From: roleoroleo <roleoroleo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Jul 2026 08:28:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] onvif: allow PTZ cameras without zoom capability

Add a PTZ zoom capability flag for text and JSON configuration.
Auto-detect zoom support from existing zoom commands or Z-axis
ranges when the flag is omitted. Use no-zoom PTZ response templates
so ONVIF clients do not see zoom spaces for pan/tilt-only cameras.

Some pan/tilt cameras expose PTZ through ONVIF but do not have
optical or digital zoom commands. Without this change, they still
advertise zoom spaces, so clients such as Frigate show zoom controls
that do not work.

Backported from upstream roleoroleo/onvif_simple_server PR #62.

Signed-off-by: roleoroleo <roleoroleo@users.noreply.github.com>

---
